Skunk[ cabbage] is one of the first plants you'll see in Spring here in New England, especially if you have any moist,[ bog]gy areas near you. You'll see the liverish-colored protective[ buds] shooting up through the snow before most other plants, because it won't take no for an answer--it produces it's own heat (60 degrees!) and melts its way through that white crap. Who needs Spring when you can make it yourself? Eventually you'll see the yellow clump of complex flowers and then all the[ cabbage]y leaves.
Of course, it gets its name because it smells like skunk. Or decaying flesh. Or both. I guess when you smell that bad it hardly matters.

